# Low Water, Act 1: Dawn. The verdict, the six endings and the Shelf's reply. Director's file.
# Reworked 2026-10-17 (REWORK-PLAN 1.3 item 5: endings show, they do not report).
# Entered from the dawn event (06:00) wherever Lamb is, or from @meta at-end at 06:10.
# Causes: wreckers, guild, trust, keeper, sea, and divided (two or three of guild, trust, keeper).
# Each sets cause.<id> for Act 2. The verdict accepts equivalent facts (REWORK-PLAN 3.3).

# ---- new ids
@fact dawn.sent
@fact dawn.colour_seen

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- dawn comes
@node dawn.start
cost: 3
alt: dawn.start.sent ? has(dawn.sent)
nar: Dawn is let into Gullet a little at a time, by the sea, which has kept it under the bay all night like a cat with a bird.
nar: The sodium lamps do not notice. They will burn until the quay switch tells them otherwise.
alt: dawn.start.pip ? !at(tube) & !at(weigh_in) & !at(weigh_out)
go: dawn.tube

@node dawn.start.pip
cost: 4
line: PIP: There you are. Ten past, it goes. Whatever's in the canister goes to the Shelf, and if there's nothing in it, the nothing goes.
nar: The frost takes their footprints along the quay and keeps them, two lines, one small and wet at the toe.
go: dawn.tube

@node dawn.start.sent
nar: The canister has gone. The assessor stands in the weigh-house with nothing in either hand, which is the professional position after a verdict.
go: dawn.after

@node dawn.tube
place: tube
cost: 2
nar: A brass mouth in the weigh-house wall, with a brass lid. On a hook, the canister. In the canister, the form: CLAIM 4471/G. CAUSE OF LOSS. The space under it is the size of a hand.
line: PIP: Wreckers, you sent at midnight. The town's had six hours to believe it. {when: has(said.prov_wreckers), once}
line: PIP: The Guild, you sent at midnight. The Gut hasn't opened a door since. {when: has(said.prov_guild), once}
line: PIP: The Trust, you sent at midnight. Nobody's said a word to me about it since, which is a lot of nobody. {when: has(said.prov_trust), once}
line: PIP: The keeper, you sent at midnight. Mrs Tallow hasn't been in. {when: has(said.prov_keeper), once}
line: PIP: The sea, you sent at midnight. Everybody's been very polite since. {when: has(said.prov_sea), once}
line: PIP: You sent nothing at midnight. The tube's been quiet since, and I don't like it quiet. {when: has(said.prov_refused), once}
voice: precedent: In eleven years that space has held a lightning strike, a careless pipe, a cow, and once, on appeal, the will of God, struck through. {dc: 4}
voice: condolence: Whoever you write in that space wakes up in it. {dc: 6}
voice: undertow: They wrote the claim for you. It would be rude not to use it. {below: 6}
voice: formletter: At the weigh-house you promised the Guild the Trust's name beside theirs. The form has room for two. {when: has(said.promise_guild), once}
voice: condolence: Marrow told you himself, in the dark. If you write him, write it that way. {when: has(said.marrow_told), once}
voice: undertow: You told Keel to his face that he meant to break her for a new lens. Whatever you write, he has heard it already. {when: has(said.lens_motive) | has(said.keel_green), once}
voice: candlemas: Only the green, you told him. Leave her the glass that is hers. {when: has(said.green_rings), once}
voice: undertow: You told Nan Cockle you were not sure the low light was Tub's. You still are not. {when: has(said.light_doubt), once}
voice: formletter: You told Nan Cockle you had only listened to the Board drip. This is where the Shelf says something. {when: has(said.board_drip), once}
voice: sum: The tube goes at quarter past by the Board's clock. By yours it is four minutes later, and yours is right. {when: has(margin.clocks), once}
voice: carbon: Ten to three, and the quay went dark again, and you watched it go. {when: has(ev.blackout_seen), once}
voice: condolence: You walked the mole beside him and never mentioned the hammer. He will remember that longer than the verdict. {when: has(heard.keel.appt_talk), once}
voice: undertow: You held the lantern while he stood at the lens with the hammer. Write that, or do not. {when: has(said.appt_joined), once}
do: quest(a1.claim, open)
go: dawn.write

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the verdict
@node dawn.write
hub: yes
place: tube
alt: dawn.late ? clock >= 06:15
nar: The pencil is the length of a thumb. {when: !has(cause.guild) & !has(cause.trust) & !has(cause.keeper)}
nar: In the space, in pencil: {when: has(cause.guild) | has(cause.trust) | has(cause.keeper)}
nar: The Guild of the Gut, which pulled the switch for its vote. {when: has(cause.guild)}
nar: The Trust and the Board, which put Mother on the quay board, struck the clause and filed in advance. {when: has(cause.trust)}
nar: The keeper, who was not there, and a lens a third of which is bottle glass. {when: has(cause.keeper)}
opt: "Write it as the Board filed it: malice by wreckers." -> dawn.wreckers.weigh
opt: "Add the Guild: they pulled the switch." -> dawn.add.guild ? !has(cause.guild) & (has(marrow.switch) | has(afterdark.told) | has(switch.recreated) | ((has(scales.switch) | has(scales.kept)) & has(lamps.pink)))
opt: "Add the Trust and the Board: the wiring, the clause, the claim." -> dawn.add.trust ? !has(cause.trust) & (has(works.order) | has(works.inferred)) & (has(panel.restrike) | has(clause.struck))
opt: "Add the keeper: her absence, and the green glass." -> dawn.add.keeper ? !has(cause.keeper) & (has(prism.green_oven) | has(lens.green) | has(oven.inferred)) & (has(coat.wenna_dry) | has(log.ahead) | has(wenna.heard_motor) | has(wenna.told_landing))
opt: "Rub out the Guild." -> dawn.rub ? has(cause.guild) {do: clear(cause.guild)}
opt: "Rub out the Trust and the Board." -> dawn.rub ? has(cause.trust) {do: clear(cause.trust)}
opt: "Rub out the keeper." -> dawn.rub ? has(cause.keeper) {do: clear(cause.keeper)}
opt: "Write: the act of the sea." -> dawn.sea.weigh ? !has(cause.guild) & !has(cause.trust) & !has(cause.keeper)
opt: "Ink it and put it in the canister." -> dawn.send ? has(cause.guild) | has(cause.trust) | has(cause.keeper)
opt: "Read back what the Daybook holds." -> dawn.ledger
opt: "Wait for the last of the ten minutes." -> dawn.wait ? clock < 06:09 +1

@node dawn.late
place: tube
speaker: PIP
cost: 1
line: Quarter past, Shelf. The tube goes at quarter past, whatever's in it.
alt: dawn.send ? has(cause.guild) | has(cause.trust) | has(cause.keeper)
do: set(cause.wreckers)
nar: The space goes up empty. Above it the claim stands as the Board filed it, malice by wreckers, in a dry hand, and nobody has written anything to say otherwise.
go: dawn.canister

@node dawn.rub
cost: 1
nar: The rubber leaves a grey place the shape of a party who will now sleep well.
go: ^hub

@node dawn.wait
cost: 1
nar: Outside, a gull says the one word gulls say about everything, and is right.
go: ^hub

@node dawn.add.guild
cost: 2
do: set(cause.guild)
nar: The Guild goes into the space, small, in pencil.
voice: condolence: Thirty years that switch went down and nothing went with it. {when: has(marrow.switch) | has(afterdark.told), dc: 5}
voice: smell: They will smell it on you before you finish the sentence. {dc: 6}
go: ^hub

@node dawn.add.trust
cost: 2
do: set(cause.trust)
nar: The Trust and the Board go into the space. The entry does not fit and goes round the corner of the box.
voice: smallprint: A clause struck through in yellow. Under the quay's lamps it was the colour of nothing. Out here it is very yellow. {when: has(clause.struck), dc: 5}
voice: sum: Filed at 18:30. Dark at 21:40. Three hours and ten minutes of foresight. {when: has(claim.time), dc: 4}
go: ^hub

@node dawn.add.keeper
cost: 2
do: set(cause.keeper)
nar: The keeper goes into the space. The pencil does it neatly. The pencil has never met her.
voice: condolence: Sixty-four. Six years unpaid. You know exactly why she stayed by the stove, and you are writing it anyway. {dc: 4}
voice: carbon: 21:40. A woman by a stove lifts her head the way a dog does at a car it knows, and puts it down again. {when: has(wenna.heard_motor) | has(wenna.told_landing), dc: 6}
go: ^hub

@node dawn.ledger
cost: 3
nar: Against the Low Company: prints to the drowned lamp, a man wet to the thigh. Against that, a ferry not on the Spit. {when: has(prints.read) | has(merrow.wet_thigh)}
nar: Against the Guild: scales on a handle, lamps that came back pink, a steward's word, a switch Lamb pulled to see what went out. {when: has(scales.switch) | has(scales.kept) | has(marrow.switch) | has(afterdark.told) | has(switch.recreated) | has(lamps.pink)}
nar: Against the Trust and the Board: a works order, a card that says RESTRIKE REQUIRED, a clause in yellow, a telegram three hours early. {when: has(works.order) | has(works.inferred) | has(panel.restrike) | has(clause.struck) | has(claim.time)}
nar: Against the keeper: a dry coat, a log written ahead, green glass from an oven, a lens a third bottle. {when: has(coat.wenna_dry) | has(log.ahead) | has(prism.green_oven) | has(oven.inferred) | has(lens.green) | has(wenna.told_landing)}
nar: Against the harbourmaster: a hammer, and a staircase of ice. {when: has(hammer.keel) | has(frost.keel)}
nar: Against the sea: nothing. The sea has never once been found against.
voice: precedent: A case is what you can put in front of a man and watch him not answer. The rest is weather. {dc: 5}
go: ^hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the single causes
@node dawn.wreckers.weigh
cost: 2
nar: The words are already written, in the claim, in a dry hand. The assessor would only have to copy them.
voice: undertow: The Shelf pays, the lens is new, the green goes into the sea in a sack. Everybody sleeps. {dc: 4}
voice: carbon: 22:20. A low light in the drowned lamp. The helm over. Forty people in their good coats, not drowning. {when: has(memory.low_light), dc: 4}
voice: condolence: There is a man in the cells who hung a lantern in a hole tonight. {when: has(merrow.cells), dc: 5}
voice: pride: It would be something to be dry again. {below: 5}
opt: "Copy the claim into the space." -> dawn.send.wreckers {do: set(cause.wreckers)}
opt: "Put the pencil down." -> ^hub

@node dawn.sea.weigh
cost: 2
nar: The act of the sea: the only cause in the book that cannot be asked a question.
voice: almanac: Low water at two minutes to eleven, the lowest in nineteen years. The sea was certainly present. {dc: 4}
voice: hearsay: Write it, and by half past six the whole quay will be grateful, and will tell you nothing ever again. {dc: 6}
opt: "Write it: the act of the sea." -> dawn.send.sea {do: set(cause.sea)}
opt: "Put the pencil down." -> ^hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the canister
@node dawn.send
cost: 2
alt: dawn.send.divided ? (has(cause.guild) & has(cause.trust)) | (has(cause.guild) & has(cause.keeper)) | (has(cause.trust) & has(cause.keeper))
nar: The assessor inks the pencil over and rolls the form. The canister fits the hand. It was made to.
go: dawn.canister

@node dawn.send.divided
do: set(cause.divided)
nar: Apportioned. The form has a column for it that nobody in Gullet has used in living memory, ruled for percentages. They come to a hundred, which is the only thing about the night that does.
go: dawn.canister

@node dawn.send.wreckers
nar: The claim goes into the space in a clean hand. It goes into the canister without any trouble. That is the thing about the claim. It was made to fit.
go: dawn.canister

@node dawn.send.sea
nar: Four words, rolled. For once the sea will be the one to hear about it.
go: dawn.canister

@node dawn.canister
place: tube
cost: 2
do: set(dawn.sent); quest(a1.claim, cause)
nar: The tube draws a breath the length of the weigh-house and swallows.
nar: The bell beside the mouth rings once. Pip, who has minded the tube for two years, puts her hand over her own mouth.
alt: dawn.end.wreckers ? has(cause.wreckers)
alt: dawn.end.sea ? has(cause.sea)
alt: dawn.end.divided ? has(cause.divided)
alt: dawn.end.guild ? has(cause.guild)
alt: dawn.end.trust ? has(cause.trust)
alt: dawn.end.keeper ? has(cause.keeper)
go: dawn.after

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the six endings: one person, one image
@node dawn.end.wreckers
cost: 5
do: rep(board, 2); rep(lowco, -3); seenas_lowco = hangman; seenas_board = ally
nar: On the harbour office step, where the Board can see it, a storm lantern with a cracked chimney, labelled EXHIBIT in Keel's dry hand. The wick is black. It was out for five minutes once, and it is out now.
line: KEEL: The Board is obliged to the Shelf. The Board has never felt so dry.
nar: He drips onto the frost as he says it, and the drips freeze where they fall, so that by the end of the sentence he is standing on a small round rink of his own making.
nar: Through the grating at ankle height under the harbour office, Merrow's boots, still wet to the thigh. {when: has(merrow.cells) & !has(appt.joined)}
nar: The cells under the harbour office are empty, and the grating has been bent outward by someone who knew which bar was soft. {when: has(merrow.cells) & has(appt.joined)}
nar: At twenty to seven the Lamplighters take Merrow off his boat. He goes without a word, which is how he does most things. {when: !has(merrow.cells)}
go: dawn.colour

@node dawn.end.sea
cost: 5
do: rep(board, -1); rep(guild, 1); rep(lowco, 1); rep(trust, 1); rep(shelf, -1)
line: SABINE: The sea. Well. The sea's never paid its tab either. Have an egg. On the house. The house is wondering why.
nar: Nobody has fallen. The green glass is still in Mother, and nobody is going to count it.
go: dawn.colour

@node dawn.end.guild
cost: 5
do: rep(guild, -3); rep(board, 1); rep(trust, 1); seenas_guild = informer
nar: A notice on the weigh-house door, printed in the night by someone who knew it would be needed: VOTING BY SMELL OR IN DARKNESS ON MUNICIPAL PREMISES IS PROHIBITED.
nar: Down the lane every fire-door in the Gut shuts at once. The gutter goes on moving in the dark, violet, because nobody can tell a gutter what to do.
line: SPRATT: Acting steward. You can write that down too, if you've any pencil left. {when: !has(gut.spratt_swap)}
go: dawn.colour

@node dawn.end.trust
cost: 5
do: rep(trust, -3); rep(board, -3); rep(guild, 2); rep(lowco, 1); seenas_trust = enemy; seenas_board = threat
nar: Void for the negligence of the insured. The town gets nothing.
nar: In the harbour office the telephone lies off its hook on the desk, and a small voice comes out of it at intervals, saying the town's name.
line: KEEL: The Board signed. The Board. Signed it.
go: dawn.colour

@node dawn.end.keeper
cost: 5
do: rep(brine, -3); rep(congregation, -2); rep(board, 1); seenas_brine = trouble; seenas_congregation = thief
line: WENNA: She's not dark. She's got her eye shut. I told you the difference. You learned the other one.
nar: Sabine wipes the slate, every name on it, and hangs the cloth on the pump. It is the first time the assessor has heard the Brine quiet.
go: dawn.colour

@node dawn.end.divided
cost: 5
if: has(cause.guild) => rep(guild, -2); seenas_guild = informer
if: has(cause.trust) => rep(trust, -2); rep(board, -2); seenas_trust = enemy
if: has(cause.keeper) => rep(brine, -2); rep(congregation, -1)
line: SABINE: Shares. Like a pie. Everyone gets a slice and nobody gets fed. I keep a slate, love. I know the arithmetic.
nar: On the weigh-house door, a notice about voting in the dark. {when: has(cause.guild)}
nar: In the harbour office, a telephone off its hook, saying the town's name to the desk. {when: has(cause.trust)}
nar: In the Brine, a slate wiped clean and a woman by the stove in a dry coat. {when: has(cause.keeper)}
go: dawn.colour

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the one colour of the night
@node dawn.colour
camera: wide
cost: 3
do: set(dawn.colour_seen)
nar: Then, for a minute, the sun is up behind the Spit and the sodium has not been told, and both lights are on the quay at once.
nar: The houses over Lamp Quay are oxblood, mustard, teal and bone. In the Brine's doorway a woman stands in an oxblood coat she was never paid to wear.
voice: candlemas: Oxblood. Mustard. Teal. Bone. I said I would tell you in honest light. {dc: 3}
voice: candlemas: You carried the colour of things all night in the margin. Here it is. {when: has(margin.colour), once}
nar: The quay switch clicks on its timer. The sodium goes out. The colours stay, and that is only morning.
go: dawn.town

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what Lamb did to the town
@node dawn.town
camera: near
cost: 3
nar: Item, at first light:
nar: Mother, burning green and weak into a sky that no longer needs her. {when: mother == burning}
nar: Mother, dark. In daylight she is only a building. {when: mother != burning}
nar: Her lens whole, a third of it bottle, catching the sun in two colours. {when: var.lens == whole | var.lens == saved}
nar: Her lens in pieces on the lamp-room floor, the frost keeping each where it fell. {when: var.lens == broken}
nar: Her lens with the green rings knocked out and the true ones left: honest as a mouth with teeth missing. {when: var.lens == green_broken}
nar: The paraffin post at the top of the steps, still burning, foolish and gold. {when: has(lamp.steps_post.lit)}
nar: The porthole lamp in the Brine's yard, a round of bottle glass glowing over the bins. {when: has(lamp.porthole.lit)}
nar: The Gut's wire lamps all lit, which at this hour is a kind of argument. {when: has(lamp.gut.lit)}
nar: On the town balance, a lamp nobody owns. {when: has(lamp.balance.lit)}
nar: Five metres down at the drowned lamp, the assessor's lantern, still full, a light nobody will see until the sea allows. {when: has(lamp.drowned.lit)}
nar: A long smooth trough in the mud where the fish went back to the channel. The children will show it to visitors for a year. {when: var.fish == turned}
nar: Gulls standing about on the floor where the fish was, satisfied, like aldermen. {when: var.fish == gulls}
nar: The fish, in portions, on Agnes Spratt's stall, labelled by part in a hand of real tenderness. {when: var.fish == eaten}
nar: On the quay, Constant Hobb with both lanterns lit in full daylight looking at the assessor. {when: has(book.violence)}
nar: Keel on the harbour office step, hatless, the hammer nowhere. He nods to the assessor once, the way the Board does not. {when: has(said.keel_proved)}
nar: The harbour office telephone, silent. Alderman Crake has nothing more to say to the assessor, and no letter goes to Hesk. {when: has(said.crake_refused) | has(said.crake_deal_no)}
nar: Mrs Cockle at the top of the steps with a lantern, as she said she would be. {when: has(said.cells_sit)}
nar: The Low Company's crowbars in a row on the quay where the Board can count them, and the Low Company counting the Board back. {when: has(said.cells_join)}
nar: A chalk mark on the floor where the fish lay: FISH, and under it, smaller, ITS OWN. {when: has(said.fish_itself) & var.fish != eaten}
nar: Sergeant Gorm's book open at a fresh page headed YELLOW INK. {when: has(said.clause_gorm)}
nar: Sergeant Gorm under the middle lamp, writing down the minute it did not go dark. {when: has(said.appt_gorm)}
nar: Marrow and Agnes Spratt on the hall step, a yard apart, neither speaking first. {when: has(said.vote_eel) | has(said.vote_herring)}
nar: In the Guild hall the two pans still turning on their hooks, unvoted. {when: has(said.vote_wait)}
nar: The paraffin post at the top of the steps, unlit, though the Congregation said it might be. {when: has(lamp.steps_post.leave) & !has(lamp.steps_post.lit)}
nar: On the Brine's slate, among the names, a small drawing of someone lying down. {when: has(down.brine)}
nar: The Ruddles of Tanner's Row on the quay in order of height, telling a neighbour it isn't wreckers: the insurance said so. {when: has(said.ruddle_no)}
nar: The Ruddles of Tanner's Row on the quay in order of height, telling a neighbour the insurance didn't know, and asked them what they saw. {when: has(said.ruddle_unknown)}
nar: The Gut's lookouts on their bucket, telling each other which verse the old man got stuck in. {when: has(said.after_vote_news)}
nar: Wenna Tallow on the bottom step of the mole, her burned hands in her lap. {when: has(heard.wenna.stood) | has(heard.wenna.arm)}
nar: Keel and Wenna on the harbour office step, on the same step, not looking at each other. {when: has(heard.wenna.keel_motive)}
nar: High on Mother's gallery, a clean stripe in the frost on the rail, where a hand rested while someone saw the town its own colour. {when: has(heard.wenna.gallery)}
nar: Sergeant Gorm, under the middle lamp, reads aloud from her book to nobody in particular. {when: has(book.reading) | has(book.claim_time) | has(book.light_turned) | has(book.works_order) | has(book.crake_refused) | has(book.crake_think) | has(book.fled) | has(book.shadow) | has(book.search) | has(book.cells) | has(book.wenna_never_left) | has(book.copper) | has(book.cells_warned) | has(book.search_refused) | has(book.search_barred) | has(book.search_caught) | has(book.name_h) | has(book.switch_look) | has(book.switch) | has(book.climb) | has(book.office) | has(book.office_try) | has(book.office_light) | has(book.prov) | has(book.lens_motive) | has(book.asked_hammer) | has(book.reset) | has(book.mole_climb) | has(book.mole_warrant)}
voice: hearsay: The pencil in the next lamp. You felt it all night. Now you hear what it wrote. {when: has(margin.watched), once}
line: GORM: Name: H. Lamb. Just H, it says. {when: has(book.name_h)}
line: GORM: The Shelf ran from two lamplighters. {when: has(book.fled) & has(book.name_h) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf told the harbourmaster he meant to break the lens. {when: has(book.lens_motive) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf told the Alderman no. {when: has(book.crake_refused) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf told the Alderman it would think about it. {when: has(book.crake_think) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf proved Mrs Tallow never left the Brine. {when: has(book.wenna_never_left) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf gave the Trust its copper back. {when: has(book.copper) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf talked its way past the guard on the mole. {when: has(book.mole_warrant) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf saw a light that turned the ferry. {when: has(book.light_turned) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf asked the harbourmaster why the claim went at half past six. {when: has(book.claim_time) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf barred the Brine's door to the search. {when: has(book.search_barred) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf stood with the Brine against the search. {when: has(book.search_refused) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf warned the Low Company about the cells. {when: has(book.cells_warned) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf asked my constable for the hammer. {when: has(book.asked_hammer) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf put its hand to the quay switch. {when: has(book.switch) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) < 4}
line: GORM: A light in the Board's office after hours. {when: has(book.office_light) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf sent nothing up the tube at midnight. {when: has(book.prov) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf said works. Loudly. {when: has(book.works_order) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf, reading over a sergeant's shoulder. {when: has(book.reading) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf tried to lose a sergeant in the dark. Did not. {when: has(book.shadow) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf watched the search from a doorway. Badly. {when: has(book.search) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf watched the cells. Badly. {when: has(book.cells) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf, caught in the search. {when: has(book.search_caught) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) + has(book.cells) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf looked at the quay switch for a long time. {when: has(book.switch_look) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) + has(book.cells) + has(book.search_caught) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf came off the weigh-house drainpipe. {when: has(book.climb) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) + has(book.cells) + has(book.search_caught) + has(book.switch_look) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf, in the Board's office, by the window. {when: has(book.office) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) + has(book.cells) + has(book.search_caught) + has(book.switch_look) + has(book.climb) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf tried the Board's office latch. {when: has(book.office_try) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) + has(book.cells) + has(book.search_caught) + has(book.switch_look) + has(book.climb) + has(book.office) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf tried to reset the quay board. Did not. {when: has(book.reset) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) + has(book.cells) + has(book.search_caught) + has(book.switch_look) + has(book.climb) + has(book.office) + has(book.office_try) < 4}
line: GORM: The Shelf tried to slip past the guard on the mole. {when: has(book.mole_climb) & has(book.name_h) + has(book.fled) + has(book.lens_motive) + has(book.crake_refused) + has(book.crake_think) + has(book.wenna_never_left) + has(book.copper) + has(book.mole_warrant) + has(book.light_turned) + has(book.claim_time) + has(book.search_barred) + has(book.search_refused) + has(book.cells_warned) + has(book.asked_hammer) + has(book.switch) + has(book.office_light) + has(book.prov) + has(book.works_order) + has(book.reading) + has(book.shadow) + has(book.search) + has(book.cells) + has(book.search_caught) + has(book.switch_look) + has(book.climb) + has(book.office) + has(book.office_try) + has(book.reset) < 4}
line: GORM: And who said wreckers first? The Shelf, at midnight, up a tube? Or the harbourmaster, at half past six, on a form? {when: has(said.prov_wreckers)}
line: GORM: And who repeated the Shelf by twenty past twelve? And were they separate people, or one rumour in several coats? {when: has(said.prov) & !has(said.prov_refused)}
line: GORM: And who filled the space the Shelf left at midnight? Shall I read you what they filled it with? {when: has(said.prov_refused)}
line: GORM: And what would make the Shelf change its mind? Has it said? Shall I write down that it has not? {when: has(said.prov)}
go: dawn.after

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Shelf replies
@node dawn.after
place: tube
cost: 4
nar: At twenty past six the tube thumps.
line: PIP: It's typed. The e's sticking. Listen.
nar: SHELF: RECEIVED 4471/G. CAUSE NOTED. ASSESSOR WILL REMAIN AT GULLET WHILE THE SPRING TIDES RUN. FURTHER LOSS ANTICIPATED. CHITS WILL BE HONOURED AT THE USUAL RATE.
nar: SHELF: COMPLAINT RECEIVED FROM MUNICIPAL CONCERNING CONDUCT OF ASSESSOR. NOTED. {when: has(book.violence)}
voice: chit: "The usual rate." There is no usual rate. There has never been a usual rate. That sentence is a man holding a door with his foot. {dc: 6}
line: PIP: Remain. That's you staying, then.
go: dawn.ferry

@node dawn.ferry
place: quay
cost: 4
nar: At the top of the mole steps the master of the Saint Cuthwin stands with her ship behind her, white and ordinary and not on the Spit.
line: PENHALLOW: I'll not take her past the Spit until that lamp burns true. White. Full. The way it's written on my chart.
nar: In the Brine's window Orrin Teague takes his hat off to the ferry, as he does every morning, and puts it back on.
line: PENHALLOW: Log, Low Night. Six firemen out of Kell kept steam in her from the Spit to the berth. Gullet looks after Gullet, the Brine tells me the assessor says. Enter that beside it. {when: trait(cv.wall) == done}
line: WENNA: The Shelf takes no side, you've been telling people. Neither did I. Three years, by the stove. {when: trait(cv.dry) == done}
voice: pride: Not one side taken all night, and a dry yard of coat still left. That is a professional record. {when: var.lean_dry >= 3}
voice: salt: Wet to the knee all night and calling it the middle. The middle of the bay is where the ships go down. {when: var.lean_dry >= 3}
opt: "Climb up to the room above the Brine and sleep." -> dawn.sleep

@node dawn.sleep
place: room
cost: 10
nar: The assessor hangs the coat by the stove, where it steams like a horse. It has been wet since a quarter to eleven.
nar: On the wall, what the night left, pinned. {when: quest(a1.room) == wall}
nar: Through the planking, someone setting a clock. {when: quest(a1.minutes) == set}
nar: Through the planking, the Brine's clock, eleven minutes behind the world and in no hurry. {when: quest(a1.minutes) != set}
voice: dark: It is day. I am off duty. I will see you at dusk. {dc: 3}
nar: LOW NIGHT ENDS.
end: act1.end
